      "writtenOn": "2026-09-10T17:54:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This allocates the memory through `vmalloc()`, which creates a mapping for the page in the kernel\u0027s vmalloc space, and that  mapping is unmapped when we free this. However, that is unnecessary. We can/should just grab the pages directly from the buddy allocator. Perhaps by using `alloc_page()` in `rust/kernel/page.rs` or add a `get_free_page()` invocation so we get a pointer to the page?",
